desc:mtt_dock recorder
// mtt_dock_recorder.jsfx — the loopback recorder of mtt_dock.
//
// Goes LAST in the master FX chain. Keeps the last N seconds of what passes
// the master, on all of its channels, but only while the signal is above a
// threshold: silence is never written, so the buffer holds sound only, one
// segment per burst. When mtt_dock asks, it plays that recording back into
// the master output (hold-to-listen in the dock) and hands chunks of it over
// for the drag-out to the timeline.
//
// All exchange with mtt_dock.lua goes through gmem "mtt_dock": the G_*/L_*
// slots below must match the ones in mtt_dock.lua.
//
// Several projects open, each with its recorder: every instance records into
// its own memory, and only while its project is the active one. gmem has one
// owner at a time: when the owner falls silent (its project went to the
// background, or it was removed), the instance now running takes over after
// 0.3 s and publishes its own recording (header, peaks, segments) with a new
// generation, so the dock starts over on it.
// mtt_dock protocol: 2

options:gmem=mtt_dock maxmem=128000000
in_pin:in 1
in_pin:in 2
in_pin:in 3
